---
import CalculatorLayout from '../../../layouts/CalculatorLayout.astro';
import Formula from '../../../components/Formula.astro';

const f = {
  fwd: "$$\\text{L} = \\text{gal} \\times 3.78541$$",
  rev: "$$\\text{gal} = \\text{L} \\times 0.264172$$",
};

const tocItems = [
  { id: 'how-to-use',      label: 'How to use this converter' },
  { id: 'formula',         label: 'How to convert gallons to liters' },
  { id: 'reverse',         label: 'How to convert liters to gallons' },
  { id: 'reference-table', label: 'Gallons to liters reference table' },
  { id: 'faq',             label: 'FAQs' },
  { id: 'related-tools',   label: 'Related tools' },
];

const schema = [
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "WebApplication",
    "name": "Gallons to Liters Converter",
    "url": "https://calculations.tools/conversion/volume-converter/gal-to-l",
    "description": "Convert US gallons to liters instantly. Formula: L = gal × 3.78541. 1 gallon = 3.785 L, 5 gallons = 18.93 L, 10 gallons = 37.85 L.",
    "applicationCategory": "UtilitiesApplication",
    "operatingSystem": "Any",
    "browserRequirements": "Requires JavaScript",
    "isAccessibleForFree": true,
    "offers": { "@type": "Offer", "price": "0", "priceCurrency": "USD" }
  },
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "HowTo",
    "name": "How to convert gallons to liters",
    "description": "Multiply US gallons by 3.78541 to get liters.",
    "step": [
      { "@type": "HowToStep", "position": 1, "name": "Enter gallon value", "text": "Type your gallon value in the gal field. The liter result updates instantly." },
      { "@type": "HowToStep", "position": 2, "name": "Read the result", "text": "The converted liter value appears immediately. For 1 gallon, the result is 3.785 L." },
      { "@type": "HowToStep", "position": 3, "name": "Convert in reverse", "text": "Type in the liter field to convert back to gallons." }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "FAQPage",
    "mainEntity": [
      { "@type": "Question", "name": "How many liters is 1 gallon?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "1 US gallon equals 3.78541 liters. This is the standard US liquid gallon definition. The UK imperial gallon is larger at 4.546 liters." } },
      { "@type": "Question", "name": "How many liters is 5 gallons?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "5 US gallons equals 18.927 liters. Multiply 5 by 3.78541: 5 × 3.78541 = 18.927 L." } },
      { "@type": "Question", "name": "How many liters is 10 gallons?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "10 US gallons equals 37.854 liters. Multiply 10 by 3.78541: 10 × 3.78541 = 37.854 L." } },
      { "@type": "Question", "name": "How many gallons is 10 liters?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "10 liters equals 2.642 US gallons. Multiply 10 by 0.264172: 10 × 0.264172 = 2.642 gallons." } }
    ]
  }
];
---
<CalculatorLayout
  title="Gallons to Liters Converter"
  metaTitle="Gallons to Liters Converter | Instantly convert gal to L"
  description="Convert US gallons to liters instantly. 1 gallon = 3.785 L, 5 gallons = 18.93 L, 10 gallons = 37.85 L. Enter gallons or liters - converts both directions."
  canonical="https://calculations.tools/conversion/volume-converter/gal-to-l"
  tocItems={tocItems}
  embedSlug="gal-to-l"
  schema={schema}
  ogFormula="L = gal × 3.78541"
  ogExample="5 gal = 18.93 L"
>
  <div slot="calculator">
    <section class="calculator-interface">
      <div class="calculator-container">
        <div class="calculator-header">
          <h2>Instantly Convert gal to L</h2>
          <p>Type in either field - converts instantly in both directions</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pair-inputs">
          <div class="pair-field">
            <label for="lp-a">Gallons (gal)</label>
            <input id="lp-a" type="text" inputmode="decimal" placeholder="e.g. 1" />
          </div>
          <div class="pair-eq">=</div>
          <div class="pair-field">
            <label for="lp-b">Liters (L)</label>
            <input id="lp-b" type="text" inputmode="decimal" placeholder="e.g. 3.785" />
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="pair-formula-note">1 gallon = 3.78541 L &nbsp;·&nbsp; US liquid gallons</div>
      </div>
    </section>
    <script src="/js/gal-to-l.js" is:inline></script>
  </div>
  <div slot="content">
    <div class="seo-container">
      <div class="answer-box">
        <div class="answer-box-label">Quick answer</div>
        <p>To convert US gallons to liters, multiply by <strong>3.78541</strong>. So 1 gal = 3.785 L, 5 gal = 18.93 L, and 10 gal = 37.85 L. The UK imperial gallon is larger (4.546 L) - this converter uses US gallons.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="answer-box">
        <div class="answer-box-label">Key takeaways</div>
        <ul>
          <li>Formula: L = gal × 3.78541. Quick mental anchor: 1 gallon is about 3.8 liters.</li>
          <li>5 gal = 18.93 L (water cooler). 10 gal = 37.85 L. 50 gal = 189.3 L.</li>
          <li>US gallon = 3.785 L. UK imperial gallon = 4.546 L - a 20% difference.</li>
          <li>Reverse: gal = L × 0.264172.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <h2 id="how-to-use">How to use our gal to L converter</h2>
      <p>Type any gallon value in the gal field and the liter result appears instantly. You can also type in the liter field to convert back to gallons - both directions work without pressing a button.</p>
      <h2 id="formula">How do you convert gallons to liters?</h2>
      <p>Multiply the number of US gallons by 3.78541. The US liquid gallon is defined exactly as 231 cubic inches, which equals 3.785411784 liters (rounded to 3.78541 for practical use).</p>
      <Formula expr={f.fwd} />
      <p>Worked examples: 1 gal = 3.785 L. 2 gal = 7.571 L. 5 gal = 18.927 L. 10 gal = 37.854 L. 20 gal = 75.708 L. 50 gal = 189.271 L. 100 gal = 378.541 L.</p>
      <h2 id="reverse">How do you convert liters to gallons?</h2>
      <p class="also-see">Multiply liters by 0.264172. See the dedicated <a href="/conversion/volume-converter/l-to-gal">liters to gallons converter</a> for a liters-first reference table.</p>
      <Formula expr={f.rev} />
      <p>Worked examples: 10 L = 2.642 gal. 20 L = 5.283 gal. 40 L = 10.567 gal. 100 L = 26.417 gal.</p>
      <h2 id="reference-table">Gallons to liters reference table</h2>
      <p>Standard US gallon values converted to liters, with practical reference contexts:</p>
      <div class="responsive-table">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr><th>Gallons (gal)</th><th>Liters (L)</th><th>Context</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>0.5 gal</td><td>1.893 L</td><td>Half gallon</td></tr>
            <tr><td>1 gal</td><td>3.785 L</td><td>Standard gallon container</td></tr>
            <tr><td>2 gal</td><td>7.571 L</td><td>Large water pitcher / 2-gal jug</td></tr>
            <tr><td>5 gal</td><td>18.927 L</td><td>Water cooler jug</td></tr>
            <tr><td>10 gal</td><td>37.854 L</td><td>Small aquarium</td></tr>
            <tr><td>15 gal</td><td>56.781 L</td><td>Medium fuel tank</td></tr>
            <tr><td>20 gal</td><td>75.708 L</td><td>Larger fuel tank</td></tr>
            <tr><td>50 gal</td><td>189.271 L</td><td>Barrel / large tank</td></tr>
            <tr><td>100 gal</td><td>378.541 L</td><td>Large cistern</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <h2 id="faq">FAQs about US gallons to liters conversion</h2>
      <h3>How many liters is 1 gallon?</h3>
      <p>1 US gallon equals 3.78541 liters. The UK imperial gallon is larger at 4.546 liters. This converter uses US liquid gallons - the standard in North America.</p>
      <h3>How many liters is 5 gallons?</h3>
      <p>5 US gallons equals 18.927 liters. 5 × 3.78541 = 18.927 L. A standard water cooler jug is 5 gallons (18.9 L).</p>
      <h3>How many liters is 10 gallons?</h3>
      <p>10 US gallons equals 37.854 liters. 10 × 3.78541 = 37.85 L. A 10-gallon aquarium holds about 38 liters of water.</p>
      <h3>How many gallons is 10 liters?</h3>
      <p>10 liters equals 2.642 US gallons. 10 × 0.264172 = 2.64 gal. A 10-liter gas can holds about 2.6 gallons of fuel.</p>
      <h2 id="related-tools">Related tools</h2>
      <ul class="related-tools-list">
        <li>
          <span class="tool-icon">💧</span>
          <div>
            <a href="/conversion/volume-converter/l-to-gal">Liters to Gallons Converter</a>
            <p>Reverse conversion - enter liters and get gallons instantly.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="tool-icon">💧</span>
          <div>
            <a href="/conversion/volume-converter/gal-to-pint">Gallons to Pints</a>
            <p>Convert gallons to US pints - 1 gallon = 8 pints.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="tool-icon">💧</span>
          <div>
            <a href="/conversion/volume-converter/l-to-fl-oz">Liters to Fluid Ounces</a>
            <p>Convert liters to fl oz - 1 L = 33.81 fl oz.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="tool-icon">💧</span>
          <div>
            <a href="/conversion/volume-converter">Volume Converter (all units)</a>
            <p>Convert between all volume units - ml, L, fl oz, cups, gallons, and more.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</CalculatorLayout>
<style is:global>
  .pair-inputs { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr auto 1fr; gap: 0.75rem; align-items: end; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  .pair-field label { display: block; font-size: 0.8rem; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.7); margin-bottom: 0.35rem; }
  .pair-field input { width: 100%; padding: 0.6rem 0.75rem; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.08); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.15); border-radius: 8px; color: white; font-size: 1rem; box-sizing: border-box; }
  .pair-eq { font-size: 1.5rem; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.5); padding-bottom: 0.35rem; }
  .pair-formula-note { text-align: center; font-size: 0.75rem; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.45); margin-top: 0.5rem; }
  @media (max-width: 480px) { .pair-inputs { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .pair-eq { text-align: center; padding-bottom: 0; } }
</style>